Claws Mail @VERSION@ - an email client (GTK 3) for RISC OS

Claws Mail 4.4.0 by the Claws Mail team (GPL version 3), on GTK 3 through
riscos-gtk's RISC OS backend. Secure connections (TLS) go through RISC
OS's own AcornSSL module.

POP3 and IMAP to fetch mail, SMTP to send it; mail kept in local (MH)
folders or on the IMAP server. Plug-ins and spell checking are not
included yet.

Needs
- RISC OS 5.28 or later (for AcornSSL), in a 16 or 32 bpp screen mode.
- SharedUnixLibrary, ARMEABISupport and Iconv (PackMan).
- An internet connection set up in !Configure (Network, with a name
  server for the Resolver).

Starting
- Run it: Claws Mail puts its icon on the icon bar and opens its main
  window. The first time, it asks for your name, email address and your
  mail servers (POP3 or IMAP, and SMTP), and where to keep your mail.
- Use "SSL/TLS" (pop3s port 995, imaps port 993, smtps port 465) or
  "STARTTLS" for your servers where your provider supports them: almost
  all do now. All of it goes through AcornSSL.
- IMAP: your server's folders appear in the folder list; opening a
  message fetches it (copies are kept in <Choices$Write>.ClawsMail's
  /claws-mail.imapcache). IMAP works in a thread of its own, so the
  desktop keeps going while it talks to the server.
- The icon bar icon: Select shows the main window; Menu gives Info (About
  this program), Choices... (Claws Mail's Preferences) and Quit.
- Drop a file on the icon (or on !ClawsMail in a Filer window) to start a
  new message with the file attached. Its RISC OS file type gives its
  type (a PDF is sent as application/pdf) and, if its name has no
  extension, one is added (Report becomes Report.pdf) for other systems.
- Quit (or a desktop shutdown) keeps any messages you were writing in
  Drafts, and asks if unsent mail is still in the Queue.

Where things are
- Settings: <Choices$Write>.ClawsMail (the /claws-mail directory there).
- Your mail: <Choices$Write>.ClawsMail.Mail, unless you chose another
  place when Claws Mail first started. Each message is a file.
- Messages go to <Wimp$ScrapDir>.ClawsMail.Log. Please send it, with a
  note of anything that goes wrong.

Using it
- Click Menu over a window for its menu (File, Edit, View, Message...).
  Keyboard short-cuts are shown in the menus.
- Get Mail fetches mail for your accounts; Write starts a new message;
  Send in the message window sends it.
- The server's certificate is checked by AcornSSL; Claws Mail's own
  certificate manager isn't available.

Not yet
- News (NNTP) is built in but untested; plug-ins, spell checking,
  address books other than Claws Mail's own.
- Saving attachments to a Filer window by dragging; opening attachments
  with RISC OS programs.
- Web links in messages open nothing yet.

Built with riscos-crossdev 1.3 and UnixLib 5.0.3.3.

